// A STATED LIMIT, kept executable: the port's not-yet-ported boundary is a
// difference the fuzzer must recognise from the DIAGNOSTIC the port prints, not
// from the shape of the input - it is a border the port announces in its own
// words (register #10), unlike the silent name-resolution gap of register #6.
// It must keep being counted rather than dropped quietly, or a run's totals stop
// meaning what they say.
//
// If the port ever ports this item kind, the fixture goes red and the register
// entry is re-measured instead of quietly outliving its subject.
static X: int = 1;
fn main() { println(1); }
